1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Welcome! Today, I’m excited to introduce Arc-Vault—

2
00:00:04,501 --> 00:00:09,000
a self-repaying, RWA-collateralized USDC lending protocol with embedded compliance

3
00:00:09,001 --> 00:00:13,500
built natively for the Arc Testnet as part of The Stablecoins Commerce Stack Challenge.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,500
Traditional DeFi lending protocols face two major bottlenecks when dealing with tokenized real-world assets:

5
00:00:18,501 --> 00:00:22,500
rigid manual repayment structures and disconnected off-chain compliance checks.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Arc-Vault solves both.

7
00:00:25,001 --> 00:00:30,000
By embedding compliance directly into smart contracts and utilizing continuous streams for repayment,

8
00:00:30,001 --> 00:00:35,000
borrowers can lock tokenized assets as collateral, draw USDC liquidity, and repay automatically over time.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Let's look at the contract architecture under the hood.

10
00:00:48,001 --> 00:00:52,500
Instead of relying on unverified off-chain tooling, Arc-Vault implements native smart contract primitives on Arc Testnet:

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000
AttestationRegistry.sol issues on-chain proofs verifying asset ownership and control with revocation support.

12
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:03,000
ComplianceRegistry.sol enforces KYC, AML, and investor accreditation limits on every action.

13
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:09,000
SelfPayingVault.sol manages RWA collateral deposits, USDC borrowing, and automated yield settlement.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,500
Arc Testnet leverages native USDC as gas, making borrow and settlement operations completely seamless

15
00:01:14,501 --> 00:01:18,000
without requiring secondary gas tokens for transactions.

16
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Now let's walk through the live decentralized application.

17
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:37,000
First, we connect our wallet via MetaMask to the Arc Testnet.

18
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:42,500
Before performing any financial action, our identity and accreditation tier must be verified on-chain.

19
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,500
I click Attest Myself to trigger an on-chain attestation.

20
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Once confirmed, our compliance status instantly updates to verified retail tier with designated credit limits.

21
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,500
In the deposit panel, we set 1 tRWA as collateral and request a 0.5 USDC loan against it.

22
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,000
We click Confirmation of collateral + Deposit and loan and authorize the transaction through MetaMask.

23
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,500
Within seconds, the transaction confirms.

24
00:02:13,501 --> 00:02:19,000
The protocol verifies our LTV ceiling, locks the tokenized collateral, mints the loan, and updates our vault health dynamically.

25
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,500
We can verify the state transition directly on the ArcScan Block Explorer.

26
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:38,500
As shown in transaction details, the smart contract executed depositRWAAndBorrow in under half a second.

27
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:44,500
1 tRWA was deposited into the vault, and 0.5 USDC was immediately transferred directly to the borrower's wallet.

28
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Every decision—from compliance verification to collateral ratio auditing—is permanently logged on-chain,

29
00:03:50,001 --> 00:03:54,000
offering a fully transparent and auditable trail for institutional compliance.

30
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:20,500
Arc-Vault also integrates Circle’s Programmable Wallets SDK at the architecture level to streamline user onboarding and wallet management.

31
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Looking at our system flowchart: users connect through a lightweight frontend

32
00:04:24,001 --> 00:04:27,500
that interacts with the Circle SDK to sign transactions seamlessly.

33
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,500
These signatures invoke the core Arc-Vault smart contracts, which automatically direct yield strategies

34
00:04:32,501 --> 00:04:35,500
to service active loan debts continuous-style.

35
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Thank you for watching! Check out the full source code and live demo links in the repository below.
